<h1>J.A.R.V.I.S — Project Documentation</h1>
<p class="small"><b>Version:</b> 1.0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <b>Last updated:</b> 2026-08-22 (after Phase 10.7 PASS) &nbsp;|&nbsp;
<b>Maintained by:</b> updated automatically after every completed phase</p>

<div class="box"><b>How to use this document:</b> Open in Microsoft Word (double-click).
Section 13 is the <i>living phase log</i> — every newly finished phase gets appended there,
and Section 14's snapshot numbers are refreshed. Nothing else needs manual editing.</div>

<!-- ================= 1 ================= -->
<h2>1. What is JARVIS?</h2>
<p><b>JARVIS (Just A Rather Very Intelligent System)</b> is a personal <b>AI Operating System for
marketing &amp; business</b>. You talk to it in plain language (chat UI); it plans work with an LLM,
executes through a controlled <b>tool system</b>, manages your <b>Meta (Facebook) ad campaigns</b>,
remembers facts about your business in a <b>memory engine</b>, and coordinates specialised
<b>agents</b>. Everything risky is <b>approval-gated</b>: JARVIS proposes, a human approves,
then — and only then — does the action run, exactly once, exactly as approved.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>You can ask JARVIS to…</th><th>What happens under the hood</th></tr>
<tr><td>"Create a campaign called Summer Launch, ₹/$25 daily budget"</td><td>Planner produces structured tool call → executor sees it writes to Meta → creates a PENDING approval with an exact parameter fingerprint → you get an Approvals card → you click Approve → tool runs once against the configured ad account.</td></tr>
<tr><td>"Pause the campaign cmp_123"</td><td>Same approval gate (side-effecting tool); read-only questions skip approval entirely.</td></tr>
<tr><td>"What do you remember about my client Acme?"</td><td>Memory engine retrieves stored facts (vector + metadata search).</td></tr>
<tr><td>"How much did we spend this week?"</td><td>Read-only Meta insights tools — no approval needed.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 2 ================= -->
<h2>2. Design Principles</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Principle</th><th>Meaning in practice</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>Modularity</b></td><td>Every agent/tool/integration is a self-contained module behind interfaces (<code>@jarvis/core</code> contracts).</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>API-first</b></td><td>The Next.js frontend is only a consumer of the Express API; no business logic in the browser.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Security by design</b></td><td>No hardcoded secrets; side effects require human approval; every attempt audited; AI cannot bypass financial guardrails.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Honest reliability</b></td><td>A crash or timeout never pretends success: uncertain outcomes become <code>UNKNOWN</code> and are reconciled against Meta — never auto-retried blindly.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Deterministic errors</b></td><td>APIs return stable machine-readable codes (see §9.4), never raw provider exceptions.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Test-proven</b></td><td>Every claim above has automated proof: 1,025 tests, real-PostgreSQL integration suites, shadow-DB drift checks (§11).</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 3 ================= -->
<h2>3. Technology Stack — what is used and why</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Layer</th><th>Tech</th><th>Why this choice</th></tr>
<tr><td>Language</td><td>TypeScript (strict)</td><td>One language across UI/API/packages; compile-time safety for a system that moves money.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Monorepo</td><td>pnpm workspaces + Turborepo</td><td>Fast cached builds/tests; clean package boundaries enforced by imports.</td></tr>
<tr><td>API</td><td>Node.js + Express + Socket.IO</td><td>Mature middleware ecosystem (auth, routers); sockets for streaming chat.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frontend</td><td>Next.js 14 (App Router), React, Zustand, Tailwind-style CSS</td><td>Server components + simple client state; fast dev experience.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Database</td><td>PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM (+ pgvector)</td><td>Relational integrity for money-touching data; transactions power atomic approval consumption; pgvector stores 1536-dim embeddings for semantic memory.</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI provider</td><td>OpenAI (via <code>@jarvis/ai-openai</code>)</td><td>Provider-agnostic contract layer means the model is swappable; planning uses structured Zod-validated outputs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Validation</td><td>Zod schemas in <code>@jarvis/core</code></td><td>Runtime-validated contracts shared by every package — one source of truth.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Testing</td><td>Vitest (+ Testing Library/jsdom for UI)</td><td>Fast ESM-native runner; per-package suites + cross-package integration.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Infra (dev)</td><td>Docker (PostgreSQL container <code>jarvis-postgres</code>)</td><td>Reproducible local database; integration tests run against the real engine.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 4 ================= -->
<h2>4. Repository Layout (monorepo packages)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Path</th><th>Package</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>apps/web</code></td><td>Frontend</td><td>Login/register, chat UI, <b>Approvals page</b>; stores JWT tokens in sessionStorage; never sees secrets.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>apps/api</code></td><td>Backend API</td><td>Express app: auth routes, conversations/chat, <b>/approvals</b> production endpoints, lifecycle-aware health, graceful shutdown controller, DI container.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/core</code></td><td>Contracts</td><td>Zod schemas + types everyone shares: AuthContext, JarvisRequest/Response, Tool/ToolResult, Approval, AuditEntry, <b>APPROVAL_TTL_MS</b>, shutdown-lifecycle contract, startup-recovery contract.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/security</code></td><td>Security</td><td>Password hashing, JWT access/refresh token service (refresh tokens stored hashed), RBAC permission checker, tool approval service.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/db</code></td><td>Data layer</td><td>Prisma schema + repositories (users, conversations, audit log, <b>approvals with atomic decisions</b>, <b>tool-execution journal</b>), migrations.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/tools</code></td><td>Tool system</td><td>ToolRegistry, <b>ToolExecutor</b> (validation → permission → approval gate → single deadline → journal), Meta Ads read/write tools, output sanitizer (secret redaction), budget guardrails.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/meta-graph</code></td><td>Meta integration</td><td>Meta Graph API client layer + campaign reconciliation logic.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/agents</code></td><td>Agent system</td><td>Orchestrator/planner: turns natural language into validated tool plans; agent registry.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/memory</code></td><td>Memory engine</td><td>Fact extraction, storage, validation, retrieval (v2 schema with embeddings).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/ai-openai</code></td><td>AI adapter</td><td>OpenAI implementation behind provider-agnostic interface.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>packages/config</code></td><td>Config</td><td>Typed environment loading incl. <code>JARVIS_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS</code>.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 5 ================= -->
<h2>5. Architecture at a Glance</h2>
<table class="archtable">
<tr><td style="background:#dbe8ff">📱 <b>Web App</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">(Next.js — Chat · Approvals · Auth)</span></td>
<td>→</td>
<td style="background:#dff5df">🖥 <b>API Server</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">(Express — Auth · Chat · <b>Approvals API</b> · Health · Shutdown)</span></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="3" style="background:#ffffff;border:none;height:8px"></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="3" style="background:#efe7ff">🧠 <b>Orchestrator (Agents)</b> — plan → validate → execute steps</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="3" style="background:#ffffff;border:none;height:8px"></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#ffe9ec">🔧 <b>Tool Executor</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">validate → RBAC → <b>approval gate</b> → deadline → journal</span></td>
<td style="background:#fff2d9">🛡 <b>Guardrails</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">budget caps · account allow-list · secret redaction</span></td>
<td style="background:#e6fbfb">💾 <b>Memory Engine</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">facts + embeddings</span></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="3" style="background:#ffffff;border:none;height:8px"></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#f0f0f0">🗄 <b>PostgreSQL</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">users · approvals · execution journal · audit log · memory</span></td>
<td>⇄</td>
<td style="background:#f0fff0">🌐 <b>Meta Graph API</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">the ONLY external write target</span></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>5.1 Lifecycle of one dangerous request (end-to-end)</h3>
<div class="box" style="font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:9.5pt">
User: "Create campaign Summer Launch ($25/day)"<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;1. <b>Web</b> → POST /api/v1/conversations … (JWT in Authorization header)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;2. <b>Auth middleware</b> verifies token → req.auth = {userId, role}<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;3. <b>Orchestrator</b> asks the LLM for a plan → Zod-validates the tool step<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;4. <b>ToolExecutor</b>: tool found ✓ · params valid ✓ · role permitted ✓ · risk=WRITE<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;5. No valid approval → create <b>PENDING Approval</b> (paramsHash fingerprint, 10-min TTL)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;→ response: status=<code>approval_pending</code> + approvalId (nothing executed!)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;6. Human opens <b>/approvals</b> → sees server-generated summary (never AI text):<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Create Meta campaign \"Summer Launch\" with objective OUTCOME_TRAFFIC and daily budget $25.00."<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;7. POST /api/v1/approvals/:id/approve → guards (rate-limit → ownership → hash match →<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;tool re-validate → account allow-list → budget cap → not draining) → <b>APPROVED</b><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;8. Executor retries tool → <b>atomic consume</b>: UPDATE approval→CONSUMED + claim execution,<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;one transaction, row-locked ⇒ double-click/replay can NEVER run it twice<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;9. Provider call (only Meta) → result journaled (SUCCEEDED / FAILED / UNKNOWN)<br>
&nbsp;10. If UNKNOWN (timeout mid-write) → <b>Reconciler</b> compares with live Meta later;<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;resolves SAFE_TO_RETRY or matches reality — never blind retry, never false success.<br>
</div>

<!-- ================= 6 ================= -->
<h2>6. The Approval System (heart of the security model)</h2>
<h3>6.1 Approval state machine</h3>
<table class="archtable">
<tr><td style="background:#fff8cc">PENDING<br/><span style="font-weight:normal">awaiting human</span></td>
<td>→ approve →</td>
<td style="background:#ddf7dd">APPROVED<br/><span style="font-weight:normal">authorized, unconsumed</span></td>
<td>→ execute →</td>
<td style="background:#d9ede0"><b>CONSUMED</b><br/><span style="font-weight:normal">terminal · never resurrected</span></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="5" style="background:#ffffff;border:none;height:6px"></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#fff8cc">PENDING</td><td>→ reject →</td><td style="background:#ffdcdc">REJECTED<br/><span style="font-weight:normal">idempotent · veto allowed until consumed</span></td><td style="border:none"></td><td style="border:none"></td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#fff8cc">PENDING/APPROVED</td><td>→ 10 min pass →</td><td style="background:#ececec">EXPIRED<br/><span style="font-weight:normal">reported lazily at read time</span></td><td style="border:none"></td><td style="border:none"></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>6.2 Guarantees (each proven by tests)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Guarantee</th><th>Mechanism</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>Exact parameters</b> — approving "what you saw"</td><td><code>paramsHash</code> = deterministic fingerprint of params stored on approval; recomputed &amp; compared at approve-time AND execute-time. Any change ⇒ fail closed.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Exactly once</b></td><td>Single interactive transaction consumes approval + claims execution (PostgreSQL row locks). Losers roll back with zero side effects.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Single winner</b> under concurrent clicks</td><td>Conditional <code>UPDATE … WHERE status='PENDING' AND expiresAt&gt;now</code>; verified with ×2/×5/×10 parallel requests — always exactly 1×200, rest 409 CONFLICT.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Fresh decisions</b> — TTL</td><td>ONE authoritative constant <code>APPROVAL_TTL_MS = 10 min</code> in core; expired ⇒ HTTP 410 APPROVAL_EXPIRED.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Human-readable truth</b></td><td>Action summaries generated deterministically <i>on the server</i> from stored params; AI prose never used as source of truth; account ids redacted (<code>act_111••••1111</code>).</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Nothing lost during deploys</b></td><td>Approving during shutdown drain ⇒ 503 EXECUTION_DRAINING and the approval stays PENDING — decidable again after restart.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Financial caps</b> the AI cannot bypass</td><td>Budget guardrails live in <code>@jarvis/tools</code> (single authority): max daily $10,000 · increase ≤25% and ≤$2,500 · decrease ≤50% and ≤$5,000 — re-checked at decision time ⇒ APPROVAL_BUDGET_EXCEEDED.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Only your account</b></td><td>Target <code>accountId</code> must equal server-configured <code>META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID</code> at decision time ⇒ ACCOUNT_UNAUTHORIZED.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 7 ================= -->
<h2>7. Reliability Engineering</h2>
<h3>7.1 Execution Journal (durable ledger for every external action)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Who may change it</th></tr>
<tr><td>PENDING / APPROVED</td><td>Created; waiting for approval / authorized</td><td>Executor, approval decision</td></tr>
<tr><td>EXECUTING</td><td>Claimed with owner + lease + heartbeat</td><td>Owner worker only</td></tr>
<tr><td>SUCCEEDED / FAILED</td><td>Certain outcomes</td><td>Terminal</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>UNKNOWN</b></td><td>Transport ambiguity (timeout/abort/crash) — write MAY have happened</td><td>Only Reconciliation resolves it</td></tr>
<tr><td>RECONCILING</td><td>Leased comparison against live Meta in progress</td><td>Reconciler (stale lease recoverable)</td></tr>
<tr><td>SAFE_TO_RETRY</td><td>Proved nothing happened (or safe class) — retry allowed with NEW approval if required</td><td>Reconciler</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>7.2 Crash &amp; deploy safety</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Startup recovery</b> (idempotent, runs before listen): stale EXECUTING → UNKNOWN; stale RECONCILING → UNKNOWN. Resolved records are never touched; UNKNOWN stays reconciliation-eligible. A dead process therefore leaves honest residue, never fake FAILED.</li>
<li><b>Graceful shutdown</b> (<code>SIGINT/SIGTERM</code>): forward-only lifecycle — stop admitting NEW write work (read-only still served), wait (bounded by <code>JARVIS_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS</code>, default 30 s, cap 10 min) for in-flight executions via an in-flight registry, then close HTTP, sockets, DB. In-flight work is never interrupted; ambiguous writes remain UNKNOWN by design.</li>
<li><b>One authoritative deadline</b> per execution: a single AbortController owns timeout; the SAME abort signal propagates executor → tool → provider → fetch, so the underlying request is truly cancelled — while the journal still records honest UNKNOWN if the wire was already cut.</li>
<li><b>Reconciliation</b> (Phase 10.5): compares UNKNOWN records against live Meta campaigns; deterministic classification into SAFE_TO_RETRY / matched-reality; attempts counted; lease-protected.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ================= 8 ================= -->
<h2>8. Authentication, Sessions &amp; Frontend Security</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Implementation</th></tr>
<tr><td>Login/Register</td><td>Email+password; passwords hashed (bcrypt-class) in <code>@jarvis/security</code>; roles (VIEWER…) drive RBAC permissions per tool resource/action.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tokens</td><td>Short-lived <b>JWT access token</b> + long-lived <b>refresh token stored hashed</b> in DB (revocable). Frontend keeps them in sessionStorage and sends <code>Authorization: Bearer …</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Identity source of truth</td><td>ONLY the verified JWT (<code>req.auth</code>). Body/path-supplied user ids are ignored everywhere — this kills IDOR by construction (foreign resources look like 404, anti-enumeration).</td></tr>
<tr><td>CSRF posture</td><td>Not applicable by design: tokens travel in a header, never cookies, so browsers cannot attach them implicitly cross-site. (Documented per spec §13.)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Output hygiene</td><td>Output sanitizer strips anything resembling secrets (<code>sk-…</code>, <code>EAA…</code> tokens, keys) from tool results before they reach users/logs; approval responses and audit entries are asserted secret-free by tests.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Secrets on disk</td><td>All credentials in <code>.env</code>, which is gitignored (verified); repo scans for key patterns come back clean except intentional fake fixtures inside redaction-test files.</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 9 ================= -->
<h2>9. Production Approval API</h2>
<h3>9.1 Endpoints</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Method &amp; path</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/approvals</code></td><td>List OWN approvals</td><td>Filters: pending/approved/consumed/rejected/expired/all · pagination (limit capped 100, server-side)</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>GET /api/v1/approvals/:id</code></td><td>Detail + summary + execution link</td><td>Shows exact params, budget, redacted account, expiry, latest execution status</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/approvals/:id/approve</code></td><td>Authorize once</td><td>Full guard chain below; single-winner</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/approvals/:id/reject</code></td><td>Veto</td><td>Idempotent; legal until consumed</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>9.2 Approve guard chain (order matters)</h3>
<div class="box mono" style="font-size:9.5pt">
rate limit → malformed id (404) → scoped fetch (404 if foreign/missing) → recomputed paramsHash<br>
vs stored (409 PARAMS_MISMATCH) → tool still exists &amp; validates (409) → configured account<br>
matches target (403) → budget guardrails (409) → not draining for WRITE tools (503) →<br>
atomic conditional transition → 200 approved | 409 conflict/consumed/rejected | 410 expired<br>
</div>
<h3>9.3 Rate limiting (multi-instance safe)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Bucket</th><th>Limit</th><th>Window</th></tr>
<tr><td>approve</td><td>20</td><td>60 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>reject</td><td>20</td><td>60 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>list</td><td>120</td><td>60 s</td></tr>
</table>
<p class="small">Counted from the shared PostgreSQL AuditLog (not in-memory) so limits hold across all processes;
every throttled attempt is itself audited (abuse trail). Trade-off documented: O(window) scan — fine for human traffic.</p>
<h3>9.4 Deterministic error codes</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>HTTP</th><th>Code</th><th>When</th></tr>
<tr><td>401</td><td>AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED</td><td>Missing/invalid bearer token</td></tr>
<tr><td>403</td><td>APPROVAL_ACCOUNT_UNAUTHORIZED</td><td>Target ≠ configured ad account</td></tr>
<tr><td>404</td><td>APPROVAL_NOT_FOUND</td><td>Missing OR foreign (existence hidden)</td></tr>
<tr><td>409</td><td>APPROVAL_PARAMS_MISMATCH</td><td>Params ≠ recorded hash / no longer valid</td></tr>
<tr><td>409</td><td>APPROVAL_ALREADY_CONSUMED</td><td>Already executed once</td></tr>
<tr><td>409</td><td>APPROVAL_ALREADY_REJECTED</td><td>Approving a rejected item</td></tr>
<tr><td>409</td><td>APPROVAL_BUDGET_EXCEEDED</td><td>Guardrail violation at decision time</td></tr>
<tr><td>409</td><td>APPROVAL_CONFLICT</td><td>Lost a concurrent race</td></tr>
<tr><td>410</td><td>APPROVAL_EXPIRED</td><td>TTL passed</td></tr>
<tr><td>429</td><td>RATE_LIMITED</td><td>Window exceeded</td></tr>
<tr><td>503</td><td>EXECUTION_DRAINING</td><td>Shutdown in progress (not consumed!)</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ================= 10 ================= -->
<h2>10. Frontend — Approvals UX</h2>
<ul>
<li><code>/approvals</code> page: status filter tabs (Pending default), paginated cards, loading / empty / error states.</li>
<li>Each card: tool id badge, <b>server-generated action sentence</b>, redacted account, formatted budget, expiry timestamp, display-only JSON parameters, Approve/Reject buttons.</li>
<li>States handled: idle → approving/rejecting (busy, buttons disabled) → approved / rejected (success message, controls removed) → <b>conflict</b> ("already handled") → <b>expired</b> → generic error.</li>
<li><b>Editing parameters is intentionally impossible</b> — changing a proposal = reject + new proposal (new hash). No edit affordance exists; tests assert its absence.</li>
<li>UI tests cover: pending render, approve success, conflict message, expired state, reject flow, page loading/error/empty.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ================= 11 ================= -->
<h2>11. Testing &amp; Verification Strategy</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Suite</th><th>Tests</th><th>Highlights</th></tr>
<tr><td>packages/core</td><td>44</td><td>Contract/schema unit tests</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/security</td><td>27</td><td>Tokens, hashing, RBAC</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/tools</td><td>534</td><td>Executor paths, Meta tools, sanitizer, guardrails, shutdown gating</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/meta-graph</td><td>99</td><td>Client + reconciliation service</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/agents</td><td>66</td><td>Orchestration/planning</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/memory</td><td>76</td><td>Extraction/validation/retrieval</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/ai-openai</td><td>3</td><td>Adapter smoke</td></tr>
<tr><td>packages/db</td><td>79</td><td>Repositories incl. <b>real-PG</b> integration: concurrent approvals, consumption atomicity, recovery, reconciliation</td></tr>
<tr><td>apps/api</td><td>65</td><td>Auth, chat, health/shutdown, <b>approval API incl. IDOR/concurrency/rate-limit/secrets + §18 real-write-safety chain</b> (endpoint → executor → mock provider with global fetch spy proving ZERO outbound HTTP)</td></tr>
<tr><td>apps/web</td><td>32</td><td>Chat UI + approvals states (jsdom/RTL)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Total</b></td><td><b>1,025 passing / 0 failing</b></td><td>+ typecheck 23/23 projects · build 13/13 · Prisma migrate status clean</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Extra gates run each phase: <b>shadow-DB replay</b> (fresh DB ← all migrations must byte-match the datamodel — zero-drift rule), <b>madge circular-dependency check</b> (none), <b>secret pattern scan</b>, and a <b>data-integrity recount</b> (orphans must stay 0).</p>

<!-- ================= 12 ================= -->
<h2>12. Running JARVIS Locally</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Step</th><th>Command</th></tr>
<tr><td>Start database</td><td><code>docker start jarvis-postgres</code> (or docker compose up)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Install / build / verify</td><td><code>pnpm install</code> · <code>pnpm build</code> · <code>pnpm typecheck</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Migrations</td><td><code>pnpm db:generate</code> then <code>pnpm db:migrate</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Run everything</td><td><code>pnpm dev</code> (web + api)</td></tr>
<tr><td>All tests</td><td><code>pnpm -r test</code> (or per-package <code>pnpm vitest run</code>)</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>12.1 Key environment variables (.env, gitignored)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Variable</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td>DATABASE_URL</td><td>PostgreSQL connection string</td></tr>
<tr><td>META_ACCESS_TOKEN</td><td>Meta Graph API credential (server-only; never sent to clients)</td></tr>
<tr><td>META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID</td><td>The ONE ad account JARVIS may touch (allow-list)</td></tr>
<tr><td>OPENAI_API_KEY</td><td>LLM planner credential</td></tr>
<tr><td>JWT_SECRET / refresh config</td><td>Token signing</td></tr>
<tr><td>JARVIS_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_MS</td><td>Graceful-drain window (default 30000, max 600000)</td></tr>
</table>

