<!-- ================= 15 ================= -->
<h2>15. Glossary</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td>Approval</td><td>Durable record authorizing ONE execution of ONE tool with EXACT parameters (hash-bound, time-boxed).</td></tr>
<tr><td>paramsHash</td><td>Deterministic fingerprint of proposal parameters; binds approval↔execution so nothing can be swapped post-approval.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consumption</td><td>Atomic transition APPROVED→CONSUMED paired with claiming an execution; the exactly-once mechanism.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Journal</td><td>ToolExecution ledger — durable source of truth for what happened externally.</td></tr>
<tr><td>UNKNOWN</td><td>Honest "we don't know if Meta received the write" state; only reconciliation resolves it.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Draining</td><td>Shutdown phase: no NEW write admissions; in-flight work finishes; approvals stay decidable-after-restart.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shadow replay</td><td>Deploy all migrations into a throwaway DB and diff against the datamodel — catches silent drift.</td></tr>
<tr><td>IDOR</td><td>Insecure Direct Object Reference — prevented by scoping every query to the JWT userId.</td></tr>
</table>

